DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzvviieeww is the window server and desktop of the COHERENT GUI
     on the hi-res (bitmap) display.  It loads the display driver
     /ddrrvv/hhrr and the pseudo-terminal driver /ddrrvv/ppttyy, takes over
     the screen and keyboard, loads the fonts, reads the applica-
     tion catalog, puts an icon on the desktop for each catalog
     entry, and runs the desktop start-up script.  It takes no
     arguments.  At boot, /eettcc/rrcc starts it when the file
     /eettcc/wwgguuii exists - create that file to enable the GUI; it
     can equally be started by hand from the console: zzvviieeww &.

     The desktop shows icons at the top left: one placeholder per
     catalog application (no process exists behind it - clicking
     it launches the program) and one icon per hidden window
     (marked with a corner badge; clicking it restores the win-
     dow).  Every window has a 3-button mouse and follows the
     same conventions:

     mmeennuuss
