FFIILLEESS
                  /etc/wgui             if present, rc starts the GUI
                  /usr/hr/etc/apps      application catalog
                  /usr/hr/etc/rc        desktop start-up script
                  /usr/hr/icons/*.icn   icons
                  /usr/hr/fonts/*.hf    fonts
                  /drv/hr, /drv/pty     drivers, loaded at start-up
                  /wscrash              crash status of a dead server

     Each aappppss line reads _n_a_m_e:_p_a_t_h:_m_u_l_t_i:_i_c_o_n:_X,_Y - menu label,
     program, whether many copies may run (1) or one (0), the
     placeholder icon, and where a launched window goes; the last
     two fields are optional and # starts a comment.  The rrcc
     script runs at desktop start-up for anything that should be
     resident from the beginning; each command must end in &.

