DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     `zview: no hi-res display on this machine'; `zview: a window
     server is already running' (if the driver was left loaded,
     `/etc/uload /drv/hr' recovers).  If the server dies, a
     watchdog writes the wait status to /wwssccrraasshh, restores the
     text console, and reports `zview: server died -- screen and
     keyboard restored'.

NNOOTTEESS
     At most 16 windows can be open and the catalog holds at most
     12 applications.  The screen is 1024x800 pixels; windows are
     clamped to it.  Applications are best launched from icons,
     the desktop menu or the aappppss catalog rather than made resi-
     dent in rrcc: a placeholder icon costs no memory until it is
     clicked.
